    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9c12651a",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a photo of actor Robert De Niro at a film festival, juxtaposed with text that sarcastically asks if he wants to get rid of Confederate flags and statues (which are symbols of slavery and racism) — implying that Black people were present during slavery and therefore should also be removed. This is a hateful and racist trope that attempts to delegitimize the historical and ongoing struggle for racial justice by suggesting that Black people themselves are part of the problem or should be erased. The meme is designed to provoke outrage and reinforce racist narratives by falsely equating the presence of Black people with the need to remove symbols of oppression, which is a direct attack on Black identity and history. It is a form of hate speech that targets Black people by implying they are complicit in or responsible for the very systems of oppression they are fighting against.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_03aa0dd9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
